  "body": "## Problem\n\nPR #3855 (`d210c7c0d`) added an edge route to `pass_link` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/ring_links.rs`, lines 141-155). No test takes this branch. The review of #3855 found that the branch is safe: each chord passes `chord_proof` (the area, the crossings, the cut column), and the whole walk is checked against the stay-down limit before any feed is added. But untested code in a toolpath link is a risk for later changes.\n\n## Fix\n\nChoose one, and record it in `docs/decisions/`:\n1. Add a pin with a part where the straight chord is blocked and the edge route is clear. Check that the link stays down, does not overcut, and does not cross.\n2. Remove the branch, if no real part needs it.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Follow-up from the review of PR #3855 (#3824, #3825).\n- Toolpath motion is under the safety floor, thus effort:high.\n",
